USB Bulk LCD protocol (handshake, frame header, chunked EP01 OUT writes, ZLP,
PM/SUB resolution ladder for 960×320, JPEG encode rotation for 960×320 when
SUB≥5) was reimplemented from the open-source project:

  thermalright-trcc-linux
  https://github.com/Lexonight1/thermalright-trcc-linux
  Copyright (C) Lexonight1 and contributors
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0

Key reference sources in that project (not vendored as a dependency):
  - src/trcc/adapters/device/bulk_lcd.py
  - src/trcc/core/protocol.py (ENCODE_ROTATIONS / bulk_profile)
  - doc/PROTOCOL_USBLCDNEW.md

Cursor usage CSV fetch algorithm (local state.vscdb accessToken + WorkosCursor
session cookie shape) was independently reimplemented in Python after reading
TokenTracker’s documented cookie format; no TokenTracker code is copied.

Dashboard layout and rendering are original to this project.

Note: the upstream 960×320 rule (SUB ≥ 5 → encode 180°) is NOT applied; on
HydroNous R1 (PM=17, SUB=5) 0° is upright.  Rotation/mirror are user settings.

Bundled third-party binaries (vendor/lhm, unmodified, from nuget.org):
  - LibreHardwareMonitorLib 0.9.6 — MPL-2.0
    https://github.com/LibreHardwareMonitor/LibreHardwareMonitor
  - HidSharp 2.6.4 — Apache-2.0
  - DiskInfoToolkit 1.1.2, RAMSPDToolkit-NDD 1.4.2, BlackSharp.Core 1.0.7
    (LibreHardwareMonitor dependencies; see their NuGet pages for licenses)
  - System.Management, System.IO.Ports, System.Threading.AccessControl,
    System.CodeDom — MIT (Microsoft / .NET Foundation)
Loaded at runtime through pythonnet (MIT) on the system .NET 8 runtime.
